{%- comment -%}
  page.static — alternate page template (TC-083 definitive fix).

  The static content URLs (/pages/about, /pages/brands, /pages/social-responsibility,
  /pages/order-verification, /pages/shipping-returns, /pages/site-map) don't exist
  as real Shopify pages, so they 404 and render through pm-404.liquid — which
  flashed the "404 Page not found" placeholder. Shopify caches the 404 response
  hard and doesn't reliably invalidate it on theme deploys, so the theme-level
  fixes can't dependably reach it.

  Fix: create REAL Shopify pages for those handles and assign them THIS template.
  Then the URL returns a proper 200 and renders the baked static body directly —
  no 404 template, no placeholder, no flash, ever.

  How to assign (Online Store → Pages → Add page):
    - Title:    e.g. "About Us"          Handle: about
    - Title:    e.g. "Authorized Brands" Handle: brands
    - Title:    "Social Responsibility"  Handle: social-responsibility
    - Title:    "Order Verification"     Handle: order-verification
    - (optional) "Shipping & Returns"    Handle: shipping-returns
    - (optional) "Site Map"              Handle: site-map
  In the page's "Theme template" dropdown choose "static". The body content can be
  left blank — this template renders it from the handle.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'pm-static-body', handle: page.handle, fallback: page.content -%}
{%- comment -%} fire the same hook the 404 path used so any dynamic bits initialise {%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('pm:static-mounted', { detail: { handle: {{ page.handle | json }} } }));
</script>
